  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Resilience by Rehabilitating Sewage and Drainage System in Ad&#x131;yaman city and Promoting Hygiene in Syrian Refugee Camp Post-Earthquake</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project focuses on the response and rehabilitation efforts following the earthquake to replace and upgrade the damaged sewage network. The main purpose is to restore the functionality and reliability of the sewage system, addressing the specific needs resulting from the earthquake&apos;s impact. While considering the needs of the refugees camp, providing hygiene kits and conducting essential hygiene awareness sessions are imperative. These efforts will ensure that the IDPs have access to necessary hygiene materials and knowledge resulting in a safe environment and promoting the well-being of those who have been affected and displaced due to the earthquake in their journey of displacement.</narrative>
  </description>
